					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1355230#post-2375579</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1355230/a-burial-in-the-woods#post-2375579</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2015 23:50:42 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>1324229</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm glad you liked it! Most of the cool stuff was Kalinin's idea, tho. I just wordied it up.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers&nbsp;for&nbsp;if&nbsp;you're&nbsp;reading&nbsp;the&nbsp;comments&nbsp;before&nbsp;you&nbsp;read&nbsp;the&nbsp;article&nbsp;for&nbsp;some&nbsp;insane&nbsp;reason</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">In&nbsp;which&nbsp;case,&nbsp;you&nbsp;probably&nbsp;have&nbsp;bigger&nbsp;problems&nbsp;than&nbsp;spoilers.</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>The ending was a little bit of artistic license on my part; he doesn't really turn into anything <em>per se</em>. It's mostly just an indication of Nemeş' inhuman-ness and the transitory nature of the Nemeş identity.</p> <p>There was a thing. That thing became Nemeş, for a time. Then, as the battle wound down, it stopped being Nemeş and became a thing again. For now, the thing rests, and is the cause of many of the 186 phenomenon. At some point, the thing will wake up again.</p> </div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1355230#post-2375560</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1355230/a-burial-in-the-woods#post-2375560</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2015 23:05:01 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Cyclopian</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1990708</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This is A: pants-shittingly terrifying, and B: a great expansion of 186. I think I caught all of the references to the original article, but there's one thing I'm still confused about. What did Nemeş turn into at the end? My first thought was that it was related to the packs of wolves that spontaneously gathered at the site of the battle in the original article, but after thinking about it I think that connection is tenuous at best, and now I have no idea what's going on.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
